WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.861
Here are two lines made of exactly the same numbers: two thousand

00:03.961 --> 00:07.336
five hundred and eleven daily returns of the S and P five

00:07.436 --> 00:11.541
hundred. The same mean, the same spread, the same histogram. Only one

00:11.641 --> 00:14.711
of them is in the order history produced. Which one?

00:14.800 --> 00:17.599
It is A. In the real market a violent day is

00:17.699 --> 00:21.686
followed by more violent days, as an earthquake is followed by

00:21.786 --> 00:26.167
aftershocks. Shuffling keeps every number and destroys exactly that.

00:26.866 --> 00:30.349
So the size of tomorrow's move is predictable, even when its

00:30.449 --> 00:33.454
sign is not. This is the idea behind ARCH and GARCH.

00:34.533 --> 00:38.830
Measure it. The correlation of today's return with the return j

00:38.930 --> 00:43.158
days ago is essentially zero: the direction has no memory. The

00:43.258 --> 00:47.555
correlation of the squared returns is positive, and it is still

00:47.655 --> 00:51.883
there a month later. Quiet follows quiet, storm follows storm.

00:52.966 --> 00:57.844
Think of tomorrow's variance, sigma squared, as the water in a leaky bucket.

00:57.944 --> 01:01.840
A tap drips a constant omega into it every day. Each night it

01:01.940 --> 01:06.687
leaks, keeping only a fraction beta of what it held. And yesterday's shock

01:06.787 --> 01:10.551
is thrown in as a splash, alpha times the squared surprise.

01:11.633 --> 01:14.445
Watch a calm spell. Then, on day eight, a bad

01:14.545 --> 01:17.681
day: the splash is large, the level jumps, and the

01:17.781 --> 01:21.564
bucket takes weeks to drain back. Those are the aftershocks.

01:27.300 --> 01:31.790
Where does the level settle? Where the water coming in, the drip

01:31.890 --> 01:36.740
plus the average splash, equals what the bucket keeps. Solve, and the

01:36.840 --> 01:41.115
long run variance is omega over one minus alpha plus beta. It

01:41.215 --> 01:44.702
exists only while alpha plus beta stays below one.

01:45.800 --> 01:50.832
How long do the aftershocks last? Forecast the variance further and

01:50.932 --> 01:55.429
further ahead: its excess over the long run level shrinks by

01:55.529 --> 01:59.719
the factor alpha plus beta per day. At zero point eight,

01:59.819 --> 02:02.784
a shock is half forgotten in three days.

02:02.866 --> 02:05.990
For the S and P five hundred, alpha plus beta is about

02:06.090 --> 02:09.334
zero point nine seven. Push it that close to one and the

02:09.434 --> 02:13.693
memory lengthens sharply: half of a shock is still there after twenty-six

02:13.793 --> 02:17.395
trading days, about a month. Near one, it barely fades at all.

02:19.466 --> 02:23.410
Now fit the model to ten years of data. Grey needles are each

02:23.510 --> 02:28.514
day's absolute move; the red line is the GARCH volatility, computed only from

02:28.614 --> 02:32.558
the past. It rises with every storm and drains away after it.

02:32.633 --> 02:36.009
In March twenty twenty the bucket overflows: one hundred and

02:36.109 --> 02:38.907
twenty percent a year, against a long run level of

02:39.007 --> 02:42.094
eighteen. Then it drains, exactly as the leak predicts.

02:43.166 --> 02:47.229
So: big moves predict big moves, while the sign stays a coin

02:47.329 --> 02:51.185
toss. Variance is a leaky bucket, filled by a drip and by

02:51.285 --> 02:56.389
yesterday's splash. Alpha plus beta tells us how long the aftershocks ring.
